course: dictionary
lesson: 14024
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can often work out which meaning is right by reading the words around it. Maintenance is one of these words. It is a noun, and it is uncountable, so we say "some maintenance", not "a maintenance".
explain: Its first meaning is work done to keep something in good working order. «The school called the maintenance team to fix the leaking roof.» The clues are leaking roof and fix, so maintenance means the work that keeps a building in good shape.
explain: Its second meaning is about money. In the UK, Ireland and Australia, after a divorce or separation, one parent may pay money regularly to help look after the child. «Dad pays maintenance every month.» The clues are Dad, pays and every month, so this meaning is money, not repair work.
explain: Its third meaning is keeping something at the same level. «Weight maintenance means staying the same weight over time.» Try the swap test: put "keeping something steady" into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Maintenance is a noun, and it is uncountable.
fact: «Maintenance» means work done to keep a building, machine, road and so on in good working order.
fact: «Maintenance» can also mean money paid regularly by one parent to help look after a child after a divorce or separation (UK, Ireland and Australia).
fact: «Maintenance» can mean keeping something at the same level, as in weight maintenance.
fact: Useful phrases: «under maintenance» means being repaired or checked; «low maintenance» means needing little care; «high maintenance» means needing a lot of care or attention.
exercise: «The lift is under maintenance, so please use the stairs.» What does under maintenance mean? | Free to use today | Closed forever and sold | *Being repaired or checked | Being painted bright red
exercise: «Ella's mum sends maintenance to help with her school trips.» What does maintenance mean here? | A small garden shed | Keeping the same weight | Work to fix the car | *Money paid to help look after a child
exercise: «This bike is low maintenance.» What does low maintenance mean? | It needs a lot of care | It is made of gold | *It needs little care | It is very fast
test: «Regular maintenance keeps the lifts safe for everyone.» Why is maintenance important here? | So the lifts get taller | *So machines stay safe and in good working order | So the lifts can be painted | So people can stop using them
test: «Jade is careful with her weight maintenance plan.» Which meaning fits? | Growing taller quickly | Paying money to a parent | Fixing a broken tap | *Keeping her weight at the same level
exam: Which sentence uses maintenance to mean money paid after a separation? | «The maintenance team arrived at nine.» | «The lift had maintenance on Monday.» | «The bike needs maintenance before the race.» | *«Mum receives maintenance for the children after the separation.»
